<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Cleary, Stephen on Chege's Blog</title><link>https://www.curiosities.dev/cited-authors/Cleary-Stephen/</link><description>Recent content in Cleary, Stephen on Chege's Blog</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:04:04 -0700</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.curiosities.dev/cited-authors/Cleary-Stephen/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Cancellation in .NET</title><link>https://www.curiosities.dev/computer-science/programming-challenges/language-concepts/resource-management/cancellation-in-dotnet/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.curiosities.dev/computer-science/programming-challenges/language-concepts/resource-management/cancellation-in-dotnet/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cancellation is cooperative. One part of the code politely notifies the other
code that it&amp;rsquo;d like it to please stop. The responding code may immediately stop,
or continue until it reaches a valid stopping point, or ignore the cancellation
request entirely. &lt;span class="citation-ref"&gt;&lt;a href="#Cleary2022"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most code has the form:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cs" data-lang="cs"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Task&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;DoSomethingAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;CancellationToken&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cancellationToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;intermediateValue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;DoFirstStepAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cancellationToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;DoSecondStepAsync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;intermediateValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cancellationToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;hellip; where the &lt;code&gt;CancellationToken&lt;/code&gt; is passed down to whatever APIs you call. &lt;span class="citation-ref"&gt;&lt;a href="#Cleary2022"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By convention, the &lt;code&gt;CancellationToken&lt;/code&gt; is the last in the method signature:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Concurrency Concerns in C#</title><link>https://www.curiosities.dev/todo/computer-science/cancellation-c-sharp/</link><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.curiosities.dev/todo/computer-science/cancellation-c-sharp/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="cancellation"&gt;Cancellation&lt;/h2&gt;
